# Files the Linux droplet executes or parses must arrive with LF endings regardless of who
# committed them from Windows: bash exits with "bad interpreter" on a CRLF shebang, and Docker
# Compose reads a trailing \r as part of an env value — which silently corrupts a password.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.env text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
